    "body": "Fixes #7857.\n\n## What\n\n`TorchSampling.filter_logits` ran `last_token_logits.div_(temperature)` in\nthe input's dtype. For BF16/FP16 logits that\n\n  - loses precision in the scaled logit and shifts top-p nucleus membership\n    at moderate temperatures like 0.1, and\n  - overflows FP16 at temperature=0 (the divisor is floored to\n    `MIN_SAMPLING_TEMPERATURE=1e-6` → `logits * 1e6` → `inf`).\n\nIssue #7857 documents both failures on a trained Nemotron-H-8B-Base-8K through\nthe dynamic engine: BF16 rounding changes which token wins at temperature=0.1,\ntop_p=0.9; FP16 scaling overflows at temperature=0. The FlashInfer sampler\nalready pins this invariant (`scaled.dtype == torch.float32`); the\nTorchSampling path is the divergent one.\n\n## Fix\n\nPromote the working buffer to FP32 when the divisor path runs; the downstream\nsoftmax / log_softmax already promote to FP32, so this is the right dtype for\nboth sampling and log-probs. The `temperature == 1.0` shortcut still preserves\nthe input dtype and the in-place mutation guard.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew tests in `tests/unit_tests/inference/sampling/test_torch_sampling.py`\npin:\n\n  - the issue's exact BF16 reproducer (`leading` token kept, runner-up\n    masked) for both BF16 and FP16 inputs,\n  - FP16 does not overflow at temperature=0,\n  - the fixed path matches the FP32 reference (mask agreement plus\n    finite-entry value match) across several `(temperature,\\` \\`top_p)`\n    combinations,\n  - `filter_logits` returns FP32 for `temperature != 1.0` and preserves\n    the input dtype for `temperature == 1.0`,\n  - the input tensor is not mutated in the `temperature == 1.0` path.\n\n## Files changed\n\n- `megatron/core/inference/sampling/torch_sampling.py` — fix\n- `tests/unit_tests/inference/sampling/test_torch_sampling.py` — new tests",
